From 1db14a30488733b045b685a752fb45f563b94299 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:41:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vk_pipeline_cache: share pipelines that differ only in unread
 vertex attribute types

With dynamic vertex input the key holds a 2-bit type for each of the 32 vertex attributes, and
Ocarina draws the same shaders with attributes they never read switched between constant and
float. Each mix was a new pipeline, translated on the GPU thread every session (a shared
22k-pipeline cache still left ~40-60 builds a session, 10-37 ms each).

The SPIR-V only declares the generics the vertex stage reads, so the types of the others change
nothing. After translation, the pipeline is filed under its key with those types cleared (union
mask per vertex shader pair; indexed or legacy loads keep every type), draws normalize their key
with the known mask, and duplicate cached pipelines are dropped at boot. Pipelines remember the
disk key they came from so the used list still matches the cache. EDEN_NX2_VERTEX_KEY_MERGE=0
turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HmEAGe4MCAJnHoeqq7Uysk
